## Show that llvm-strings can handle a negative signed char value (i.e. > 0x7f).
## Such characters should form string delimiters like other unprintable ones,
## unless using an encoding where they form valid characters.

# RUN: printf "z\0\200\0\302\241\0a\0" | llvm-strings --encoding=s --bytes 1 - | FileCheck %s
# RUN: printf "z\0\200\0\302\241\0a\0" | llvm-strings --encoding=u --bytes 1 - | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,CHECK-UTF8
# CHECK: z{{$}}
# CHECK-UTF8-NEXT: {{^}}¡{{$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: {{^}}a
